\0
The Imperium operated a detention camp in a barren marshland region of the Rhent. A number of Freedom Guard prisoners were confined there, along with some of the more infamous civilian criminals from around the galaxy. Imperium biotic researchers there were using the prisoners for genetic experimentation. Among those held in the compound was Freedom Guard Commander Jeb Radec, who led the water raid on Alcine. The Freedom Guard assaulted the camp in an attempt to recover Radec and the others. 
\1
The Freedom Guard have established an attack base nearby. The insurgents have raided our detention facilities and released a number of prisoners. The escaped prisoners and their liberators are now fleeing the compound. An escape vessel is waiting to move the fugitives off-planet. We believe there is a convoy nearby carrying Freedom Guard Commander Radec. Find it before Radec can escape. Hunt them down and kill them all.\n
\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
--> Repair the damaged compound and hold\n
\s\s\s\s  off any diversionary counter-attacks\n
--> Track down and kill the escaped prisoners\n
--> Scout out potential escape routes for the\n
\s\s\s\s convoy carrying Commander Radec\n
--> Destroy the convoy
\2
You have done well, my son. You are stronger than I realized.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
The Freedom Guard was successful in releasing their prisoners, including Jeb Radec, the dissident leader who led the water raid on Alcine. The entire operation, however, was a carefully plotted subterfuge by the Imperium's Shadowhand Corps. Months before the incident, Shadowhand operative Stiv Baator was infected with the Marked genetic keys and introduced into the prisoner population. The Imperium then leaked the location of the detention camp, knowing that the Freedom Guard would attempt to save Radec. Baator escaped with Radec and the others and was eventually able to penetrate Radec's command. He became a trusted Freedom Guard officer and an essential source of intelligence for the Imperium.
\3
Focus, my son. You must have focus. 
